  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Background Audio is a feature of the Quest OS that let's you play any kind of music in the background, while keeping all the game's sounds still intact.\n\nIt's not a widely known feature but for those that do know how to enable Background Audio this bug is a pretty bummer. Not being able to listen to my own music (or podcast, or audio book) severely affects my VRChat experience. Please fix!\n\nDevice: Quest 3 with Quest OS PTC v65.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\nStart VRChat (Quest Standalone) -> Press the Meta button on your right touch controller to open the Quest system menu -> Open Meta web browser -> go to Spotify, play some music -> Go to your system notifications, you should be able to see a notification there from the browser  with the name of your song -> click on the three dots, press Playback -> Switch back to VRChat\n\nExpected Result:\n\nThe music should continue to play in the background while playing VRChat with all the game sounds still intact. This works on the LIVE version of VRChat (build 1436).\n\nActual Result: \n\nThe music will fade out and stop playing entirely. It doesn't work anymore in Build 1444. Game sounds still continue to play.",
